  "editorial": [
    "The rolled chords at bars 3, 5 and 7 start on beat 2. Their four notes enter bottom to top one 24-PPQ tick apart and all release at beat 3. The 3-tick spread is an editorial realization of the printed arpeggio signs.",
    "Written G-sharp4 carries through both chords of bar 19. C-sharp4 carries through both chords of bar 21. F-natural4 in bar 23 cancels the preceding chromatic color. Bar 27 has A-sharp3 in the outer chords and the explicitly natural A4 on beat 2.",
    "The identical chords joining bars 28-29 and 30-31 remain single tied attacks. Curves between changing chords are realized at nominal note values without adding pedal or slur overlap.",
    "Accent, staccato, tenuto and dynamic shaping are not synthesized. Filled noteheads with pale scan interiors are read at their stem/flag values, checked against the 3/4 bar and parallel figures."
